values ('f0a1b2c3-4d5e-4a20-9b90-0c1d2e3f4a00', 'archaeology', 'Archaeology', 'This course treats archaeology as an evidence-driven, ethically accountable study of human lives through material remains. It begins with archaeological questions and theory, moves through field, laboratory, dating, digital, and interpretive methods, and ends with applied heritage practice, CRM, public communication, and a capstone research product.');

